Single-database Alembic configuration for the Secure Flask Authentication API.

## New database

Apply the complete committed schema with:

    flask --app app.py db upgrade

## Existing database from the pre-migration project

The first committed revision represents the schema that existed before MFA was
added. If you already have that development database, mark it as the baseline
without recreating tables, then apply the MFA migration:

    flask --app app.py db stamp 20260929_01
    flask --app app.py db upgrade

Back up any database you care about before applying migrations.

## Future model changes

Create a revision with:

    flask --app app.py db migrate -m "describe the schema change"

Review generated revisions before committing them. Alembic autogeneration is a
starting point, not a substitute for reviewing indexes, constraints, defaults,
and data migrations.
